  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "In 197119711971, Chef and his wife created a beautiful array AAA  of NNN integers: A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​. The absolute difference between any two adjacent elements of the array was at most DDD. When he read about **Prefix Max** and **Prefix Min** in 200020002000, Chef made two more arrays BBB and CCC of NNN integers where, for iii ranging from 111 to NNN,\n\n\nBi=max(A1,.....Ai)B_i = max(A_1,.....A_i)Bi​=max(A1​,.....Ai​)\nCi=min(A1,.....Ai)C_i = min(A_1,.....A_i)Ci​=min(A1​,.....Ai​)\nNow it is 2023. Unfortunately, Chef has lost the original array AAA. But fortunately he still remembers the arrays BBB, CCC, and the value of DDD. He is missing his late wife and array AAA a lot nowadays. He knows you are a great programmer and so asks for your help. He has given you the arrays BBB, CCC, and the value of DDD. Can you generate his lost array AAA?\n\nIf there are multiple arrays AAA which satisfy the constraints, you can print any of them. It is also possible that it is impossible to generate an array AAA using the information Chef remembered. If so, print \"No\".\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first input line will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of 333 lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and DDD — the number of elements in the array and the upper bound on the difference between any two adjacent elements of the array.\nThe next line contains NNN space-separated integers B1,B2,…,BNB_1, B_2, \\ldots, B_NB1​,B2​,…,BN​.\nThe next line contains NNN space-separated integers C1,C2,…,CNC_1, C_2, \\ldots, C_NC1​,C2​,…,CN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case,\n\n\n\n\nIf it is possible to generate the array AAA, print 2 lines-\n\n\n\nIn the first line print **\"YES\"** without quotes.\nIn the second line print NNN space-separated integers, the array A1A_1A1​...ANA_NAN​.\n\n\n\nOtherwise, print **\"NO\"** in one line without quotes.\n\n\n\n\nYou may print each character of the string in uppercase or lowercase (for example, the strings YES, yEs, yes, and yeS will all be treated as identical).",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤2∗1051 \\leq T \\leq 2*10^51≤T≤2∗105",
      "1≤N≤5∗1051 \\leq N\\leq 5*10^51≤N≤5∗105",
      "0≤D≤1090 \\leq D \\leq 10^90≤D≤109",
      "−109≤Bi,Ci≤109-10^9 \\leq B_i, C_i \\leq 10^9−109≤Bi​,Ci​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 5∗1055*10^55∗105."
    ],
